# imp/hw_gate = the HARDWARE EVIDENCE TREE. Tracked deliberately: unlike
# imp/fpga (6.7 GB of build output) and imp/sim_gate (regenerable logs), these
# are bench runs that CANNOT be reproduced by re-running anything — md5-pinned
# deploys, ILA captures, per-run campaign logs, and the verdicts that cite them.
# Until 2026-08-14 the whole tree was untracked and single-copy, which meant no
# `in_hw_gate: true` row in the bug registry could be substantiated by anything
# a reviewer could fetch. ~9 MB, no file over 2 MB.
# Large regenerable artefacts stay excluded below — keep that list current if a
# capture format grows, and NEVER un-ignore imp/fpga.
!imp/hw_gate/
imp/hw_gate/**/*.bit
imp/hw_gate/**/*.bin
imp/hw_gate/**/*.dcp
imp/hw_gate/**/*.ltx
imp/hw_gate/**/sim_build*/

