# =============================================================================
# EDA RUN DIRECTORIES — THE SUFFIXED VARIANTS  (added 2026-08-14)
#
# THIS REPOSITORY IS PUBLIC:
#   github.com/SoC-Labs/TideLink-Chiplet-Interconnect-AHB
#
# The rules further up cover the flows whose run trees are spelled plainly, and
# fusion-compiler and primetime already carry their `*` variants. The flows
# below were still spelled bare, or not at all.
#
# WHY THE GLOB MATTERS. Every flow here takes a run suffix, so a real run lands
# in `work_12t/` or `outputs_12t_flat/` — and a bare `work/` matches neither. A
# vendor-derived netlist, .lib, .db or GDS sitting in an unignored run directory
# is one `git add -A` away from publication, and an untracked file in a
# directory nobody had ignored is exactly how this estate's two disclosures
# happened. Verified with `git check-ignore` that none of these covers a file
# tracked on this branch.
# =============================================================================
syn/asic/design-compiler/work*/
syn/asic/design-compiler/libs*/
syn/asic/design-compiler/logs*/
syn/asic/design-compiler/reports*/
syn/asic/design-compiler/outputs*/
syn/asic/design-compiler/*_dc_output/
syn/asic/design-compiler/*_dc_reports/
syn/asic/rtl-architect/work*/
syn/asic/rtl-architect/libs*/
syn/asic/rtl-architect/logs*/
syn/asic/rtl-architect/reports*/
syn/asic/rtl-architect/outputs*/
syn/asic/formality/work*/
syn/asic/formality/logs*/
syn/asic/formality/reports*/
syn/asic/formality/outputs*/
syn/asic/calibre/work*/
syn/asic/calibre/logs*/
syn/asic/calibre/reports*/
syn/asic/calibre/outputs*/
syn/asic/dft/work*/
syn/asic/dft/logs*/
syn/asic/dft/reports*/
syn/asic/dft/outputs*/

# Catch-all for a flow directory added after this list was written. The thing
# that keeps being missed is the SUFFIX, not the flow name — so these match only
# the suffixed spellings and leave a bare `scripts/` or `inputs/` alone.
syn/asic/*/work_*/
syn/asic/*/libs_*/
syn/asic/*/logs_*/
syn/asic/*/reports_*/
syn/asic/*/outputs_*/

# Simulator build products that carry a run suffix. The bare spellings (`simv`,
# `csrc`, `xcelium.d`) are already above; these are the per-run variants a
# parallel or multi-config regression leaves behind.
**/simv*.daidir/
**/csrc*/
**/xcelium.d*/
**/INCA_libs*/
**/*.vdb/
sim_build/
